# Machine lease

On the QA PC and laptop, **HEAVY** runs take `%USERPROFILE%\machine-lease.ps1` before the run and `release` after.
**LIGHT** (one vitest file, `tsc`, `typecheck:tests`) needs no lease.

Always use **`-File`**, never `powershell -Command "& ..."`, when interpreting exit codes — `-Command` loses script exit
codes (non-owner `release` is **12** under `-File`, **1** under `-Command`). Read `$LASTEXITCODE` in the same session.

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:USERPROFILE\machine-lease.ps1" take -OwnerPid $owner -Seat <seat> -TtlMinutes 90
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:USERPROFILE\machine-lease.ps1" release -OwnerPid $owner
```

Cursor seats (D-118a): `$owner` = nearest `cursor-agent` ancestor; same pid for take and release. `take` with a dead pid
exits **2**.
